  m_text: A rope bridge is a suspension structure built from ropes and wooden planks
    to span gaps like rivers or ravines. Traditionally, these were made from natural
    fibers for crossing treacherous terrain. Today, they are popular in playgrounds
    for balance training or, using steel cables, built as durable pedestrian crossings.
